WEBVTT

01:16.285 --> 01:18.620
- Hello?
- How dare you make my son cry.

01:19.329 --> 01:20.329
Laxmi?

01:20.330 --> 01:21.706
You made everyone cry.

01:21.707 --> 01:24.709
And you gave your chaperone
a heart attack. What is wrong with you?

01:24.710 --> 01:28.546
First of all, I don't have a chaperone,
so stop calling her that.

01:28.547 --> 01:31.757
Second of all, Zosia's gonna be fine,
thank you for asking.

01:31.758 --> 01:34.302
- And third of all--
- Why do you do such things?

01:34.303 --> 01:35.595
Are you mentally unsound?

01:35.596 --> 01:40.100
Third of all,
I learned something important.

01:40.684 --> 01:42.351
Laxmi, I think that
there might be a way to fix--

01:42.352 --> 01:45.230
You do not ever make my son cry again.

01:53.572 --> 01:56.115
Hey, if Miss Sunshine asks
for my phone number again,

01:56.116 --> 01:57.618
you tell her to pound sand.

02:17.179 --> 02:18.931
She's gonna be all right, isn't she?

02:19.848 --> 02:21.058
She's gonna be fine.

05:35.836 --> 05:36.879
Hello?

05:53.187 --> 05:54.646
Anybody here?

05:59.234 --> 06:00.318
- Hello, Carol.
- Hey.

06:00.319 --> 06:02.487
- Where did everybody--
- This is a recording.

06:03.071 --> 06:07.074
At the tone, you can leave a message
to request anything you might need.

06:07.075 --> 06:08.660
We'll do our best to provide it.

06:09.536 --> 06:12.622
Our feelings for you
haven't changed, Carol.

06:12.623 --> 06:16.543
But after everything that's happened,
we just need a little space.

07:18.355 --> 07:19.356
Come on.

07:38.000 --> 07:40.169
Are you fucking kidding me?

07:44.047 --> 07:45.048
Fine.

07:46.800 --> 07:48.218
Good riddance!

07:50.762 --> 07:51.889
Fuck you!

08:44.650 --> 08:47.486
Afflicted... Afflicted people.

09:56.805 --> 10:00.516
To my 12 fellow survivors, greetings.

10:00.517 --> 10:02.268
I'm Carol Sturka.

10:02.269 --> 10:05.272
Some of you know me.
Some of you I've yet to meet.

10:05.856 --> 10:07.024
But...

10:07.900 --> 10:09.234
if you're still one of us...

10:10.444 --> 10:12.070
then this message is for you.

10:14.823 --> 10:17.576
There is a way to undo this situation.

10:18.243 --> 10:21.413
To turn the world back
the way it's supposed to be.

10:24.499 --> 10:25.501
How do I know this?

10:26.001 --> 10:28.503
Because earlier today,

10:28.504 --> 10:33.759
these afflicted people, these Others,
they basically told me so themselves.

10:34.510 --> 10:38.555
Because guess what? They can't lie.

10:40.098 --> 10:42.017
Which is yet another thing
I've discovered.

10:42.809 --> 10:45.062
This alien virus, or...

10:45.604 --> 10:49.733
whatever it is,
it doesn't allow them to do that.

10:51.068 --> 10:55.280
So, what is this solution exactly?

10:56.907 --> 10:58.325
That they didn't tell me.

10:58.992 --> 11:05.415
But they so resisted telling me,
that everybody suddenly burst into tears.

11:06.083 --> 11:08.460
Worldwide, apparently.

11:09.545 --> 11:11.296
Which I know upset at least one of you.

11:12.005 --> 11:16.844
And then after that, they completely
abandoned the city I live in.

11:17.970 --> 11:20.264
Leaving me here all alone.

11:21.765 --> 11:24.184
Which says to me I'm on the right track.

11:25.853 --> 11:29.857
Now, I realize some of you

11:30.774 --> 11:33.151
think the world might be
better off this way,

11:33.735 --> 11:36.488
with all the newfound peace,
love and understanding.

11:37.656 --> 11:39.116
Enjoy that opinion.

11:40.200 --> 11:41.285
Relish it.

11:42.077 --> 11:44.329
Because it may be
the last one you ever possess.

11:44.913 --> 11:46.414
And when the day comes

11:46.415 --> 11:49.667
that you have peace and love
forced upon you, who knows,

11:49.668 --> 11:51.837
maybe in that last fleeting moment

11:52.796 --> 11:56.633
you might just realize
you treasured your individuality.

11:58.886 --> 12:01.388
Please, let's work together.

12:02.431 --> 12:03.432
The 13 of us.

12:03.932 --> 12:05.809
'Cause it's gonna take
everything we've got.

12:06.852 --> 12:10.063
But these people need saving.

12:12.816 --> 12:14.234
We owe it to humanity.

12:16.778 --> 12:19.239
Call me anytime, day or night.

12:21.283 --> 12:22.701
Good luck and godspeed.

12:43.013 --> 12:44.514
Hello, Carol.

12:44.515 --> 12:46.016
This is a recording.

12:46.642 --> 12:50.520
At the tone, you can leave a message
to request anything you might need.

12:50.521 --> 12:53.231
- Yes, yes.
- We'll do our best to provide it.

12:53.232 --> 12:54.690
- Our feelings for you...
- Got it.

12:54.691 --> 12:56.150
- ...haven't changed, Carol.
- Got it.

12:56.151 --> 12:58.070
- Got it.
- But after everything that's happened,

12:58.654 --> 13:00.614
- we just need a little space.
- Got it.

13:02.658 --> 13:03.950
It's Carol.

13:03.951 --> 13:05.452
I've made a video.

13:05.994 --> 13:07.245
You're not gonna like it.

13:07.246 --> 13:09.789
However, I want you to make 12 copies

13:09.790 --> 13:12.917
and distribute them
to all of the other people like me.

13:12.918 --> 13:14.418
And for those that don't speak English,

13:14.419 --> 13:18.006
I want you to subtitle what I say
word-for-word.

13:19.424 --> 13:20.842
I certainly can't force you to do this.

13:20.843 --> 13:24.847
However, you doing it would please me,
and I know you're into that.

13:26.473 --> 13:29.601
And conversely, if you don't do it,

13:30.686 --> 13:33.396
I can't be held responsible
for the biblically shitty mood

13:33.397 --> 13:35.440
in which I will no doubt find myself.

13:36.984 --> 13:41.488
So, I'm gonna leave it outside
on the curb, by a rock.

13:42.281 --> 13:45.951
And I'll stay far, far away
'cause God knows you need your space.

16:59.561 --> 17:01.855
No. No. No, no, no.

17:23.085 --> 17:24.086
Hey!

17:26.255 --> 17:27.506
Get out of here!

18:09.631 --> 18:10.632
Hello, Carol.

18:11.341 --> 18:12.718
This is a recording.

18:13.343 --> 18:16.889
At the tone, you can leave a message
to request anything you might need.

18:17.472 --> 18:19.141
We'll do our best to provide it.

18:20.184 --> 18:22.394
Our feelings for you
haven't changed, Carol.

18:23.061 --> 18:26.648
But after everything that's happened,
we just need a little space.

18:29.484 --> 18:32.446
I want the lights back on. All of them.

18:33.280 --> 18:34.281
Everywhere.

18:34.948 --> 18:36.158
Now.

19:39.847 --> 19:41.472
Hello, Carol.

19:41.473 --> 19:43.349
This is a recording.

19:43.350 --> 19:47.229
At the tone, you can leave a message
to request anything you might need.

19:47.771 --> 19:49.398
We'll do our best to provide it.

19:50.023 --> 19:53.150
Our feelings for you
haven't changed, Carol.

19:53.151 --> 19:56.864
But after everything that's happened,
we just need a little space.

19:59.950 --> 20:01.577
I need my trash picked up.

20:31.273 --> 20:32.274
Hello.

20:32.858 --> 20:34.234
Hello, Carol.

20:34.735 --> 20:35.944
This is a recording.

20:36.987 --> 20:39.739
We can pick up your trash
as long as it's bagged,

20:39.740 --> 20:42.367
and each bag weighs 17 pounds or less.

20:42.993 --> 20:44.744
Please remove all bags from the bin

20:44.745 --> 20:48.080
and place them on the curb
a minimum of two feet apart.

20:48.081 --> 20:49.166
Thank you.

24:30.012 --> 24:32.055
You motherfuckers sure love your milk.

26:21.832 --> 26:22.916
Hello!

26:31.842 --> 26:32.843
Hello?

26:43.812 --> 26:45.355
Shoo! Hey!

26:45.856 --> 26:47.399
Shoo! Get out of there!

27:56.969 --> 27:58.928
Greetings, fellow survivors.

27:58.929 --> 28:01.180
Carol Sturka here with an update.

28:01.181 --> 28:03.809
Here where I live,
Albuquerque, New Mexico,

28:04.476 --> 28:07.728
they drink this
like it's going out of style.

28:07.729 --> 28:11.023
These are little milk cartons,

28:11.024 --> 28:13.443
the kind we give children
in elementary schools.

28:13.944 --> 28:15.571
Back when we had elementary schools.

28:16.071 --> 28:17.280
And children.

28:17.281 --> 28:20.616
And, as you can see,
they seem to come in all kinds of flavors.

28:20.617 --> 28:23.286
Plain, chocolate, strawberry, so on.

28:23.287 --> 28:24.580
But the thing is,

28:25.497 --> 28:27.749
it's not milk in any of them.

28:29.293 --> 28:35.382
It is this one strange liquid.

28:39.094 --> 28:42.680
And they make it
in this local dairy facility in my town.

28:42.681 --> 28:45.057
Well, made. Past tense.

28:45.058 --> 28:47.018
'Cause as I told you in my previous video,

28:47.019 --> 28:49.770
they've shut everything down here
and abandoned me completely.

28:49.771 --> 28:52.899
Which is... You know, whatever. Who cares?

28:52.900 --> 28:57.654
But in this dairy,
they make this by mixing water

28:58.238 --> 28:59.281
into...

29:01.033 --> 29:07.246
this white powdery stuff.

29:07.247 --> 29:08.539
Can you see that?

29:08.540 --> 29:10.042
Whatever that is.

29:10.626 --> 29:13.504
And then the resulting liquid is
all they seem to consume.

29:14.713 --> 29:16.089
Look around where you live.

29:16.590 --> 29:20.510
I'll bet they are manufacturing
this in every city in the world.

29:20.511 --> 29:24.306
Everywhere there's a spare dairy
or a bottling factory.

29:24.806 --> 29:27.141
Maybe where you are, it doesn't come
in a carton, it comes in a can,

29:27.142 --> 29:29.520
but either way, it's this.

29:31.730 --> 29:32.814
So what is this?

29:35.234 --> 29:37.652
What does it do to them
when they drink it?

29:37.653 --> 29:40.864
Could it be that this is
how they're all staying connected?

29:42.950 --> 29:44.326
Here's what I know so far.

29:45.494 --> 29:47.120
It does not smell like anything.

29:48.622 --> 29:52.835
But it's got this weird texture.

29:55.003 --> 29:58.090
It's kind of like olive oil, but thinner.

29:58.590 --> 30:00.008
That probably means something.

30:01.301 --> 30:03.928
And I've got no idea
what makes it this color.

30:03.929 --> 30:05.764
What would you call that? Amber?

30:06.640 --> 30:07.891
Straw? Straw colored?

30:08.559 --> 30:11.644
And I tested the pH. It is a 7.1,

30:11.645 --> 30:13.020
which means...

30:13.021 --> 30:14.731
Hang on, I have it marked.

30:15.274 --> 30:16.275
It is

30:17.484 --> 30:18.485
neutral.

30:19.528 --> 30:21.655
Well, basically, it's neutral.

30:22.990 --> 30:24.282
You know what else is neutral?

30:24.283 --> 30:25.367
Celery.

30:26.535 --> 30:28.620
And water, so...

30:31.164 --> 30:32.165
Yeah.

30:36.753 --> 30:39.423
And it does not contain chlorine.

30:40.674 --> 30:41.675
So...

30:44.803 --> 30:46.470
Anybody listening out there?

30:46.471 --> 30:47.889
Huh? How about it, you 12?

30:47.890 --> 30:49.433
Any response?

30:50.434 --> 30:53.520
Are you even getting these?
'Cause how the fuck would I know?

31:32.643 --> 31:34.185
Greetings, fellow survivors.

31:34.186 --> 31:36.313
Carol Sturka here with an update.

33:02.274 --> 33:03.609
No.

33:05.569 --> 33:06.570
No!

33:09.573 --> 33:11.408
Get away from there!

33:12.993 --> 33:13.994
Hey!

33:22.836 --> 33:24.922
Fuck.

33:48.862 --> 33:52.741
Why won't you fucking come loose?

35:30.255 --> 35:31.632
Son of a bitch.

35:57.115 --> 35:58.784
Son of a bitch.
